 "comment": "clause44: what the module check catches. A voucher whose PARTYGSTIN is only spaces reads as no GSTIN in the walk (the reference strips it after choosing it over the ledger's) but the check falls back to the ledger's GSTIN; a regular voucher whose GUID a later cancelled voucher with an unregistered party repeats (the check reads the last voucher with a GUID); two regular vouchers sharing a GUID, one unregistered and one registered (each column cites the GUID once, labelled by its own first row); a line on a ledger with no master; a party that is a sales ledger. GSTINs invented (fourteenth character Y).",
